%[text] %[text:anchor:H_0A3CB15A] ## **Complex-Valued Functions** 
%[text] Real-valued functions are only one special case of the more general complex Fourier series. Indeed, the complex Fourier series can represent a wide variety of complex functions. A complex function has a real and imaginary component:
%[text]{"align":"center"} $f(t) = f\_{re}(t) + i f\_{im}(t)${"altText":"f(t) = f\_{re}(t) + i f\_{im}(t)"}
%[text]  ![interact](text:image:7603) **Activity**. The lemniscate is a figure-8 curve that can be described with just four modes of the complex Fourier series. In this activity, you will draw a lemniscate in the app. The lemniscate can be described by the complex-valued function
%[text]{"align":"center"} $f(t) = \\cos (2 \\pi t) + \\frac{i}{2} \\sin (4 \\pi t)${"altText":"f(t) = \cos (2 \pi t) + \frac{i}{2} \sin (4 \pi t)"}
%[text] **Task 1.** Run the Complex Fourier Series app.
%[text]{"align":"center"} [![cover app](text:image:7789)](<matlab: run ComplexFourierSeries>)
%[text]{"align":"center"} [ComplexFourierSeriesApp.mlapp](<matlab: run ComplexFourierSeriesApp>)
%[text] **Task 2.** The first two modes of the lemniscate describe a real cosine curve with a frequency of 1 Hz. Adjust the Fourier coefficients to create the graph of the real cosine shown below.
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![realCosine screenshot](text:image:6fa8)
%[text] **Task 3.** Adjust the coefficients for the $n = 2${"altText":"n = 2"} mode to create the imaginary component of the function: $ \\frac{i}{2} \\sin (4 \\pi t)${"altText":" \frac{i}{2} \sin (4 \pi t)"}. If correct, the complex plot should show the lemniscate.
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![lemniscate screenshot](text:image:8972)
%[text] 
%[text] **Task 4**. Animate the plot. 
%%
%[text] ![write ](text:image:1de6) **Exercise.** Use the integration formula
%[text]{"align":"center"} $c\_n = \\frac{1}{2L} \\int\_{-L}^{L} y(t) e^{ -\\frac{i n \\pi}{L} t} dt${"altText":"c\_n = \frac{1}{2L} \int\_{-L}^{L} y(t) e^{ -\frac{i n \pi}{L} t} dt"}
%[text] with $L = 0.5${"altText":"L = 0.5"} (to match the definition in the app) to derive the complex series coefficients for the lemniscate function:
%[text]{"align":"center"} $f(t) = \\cos (2 \\pi t) + \\frac{i}{2} \\sin (4 \\pi t)${"altText":"f(t) = \cos (2 \pi t) + \frac{i}{2} \sin (4 \pi t)"}
%[text] Do they match the result that you found in the activity?
%[text] **Hint**: start by rewriting the sines and cosines in terms of complex exponentials using the formulas:
%[text]{"align":"center"} $\\cos \\theta = \\frac{e^{i \\theta} + e^{- i \\theta}}{2}${"altText":"\cos \theta = \frac{e^{i \theta} + e^{- i \theta}}{2}"}    and    $\\sin \\theta = \\frac{e^{i \\theta} - e^{- i \\theta}}{2i}${"altText":"\sin \theta = \frac{e^{i \theta} - e^{- i \theta}}{2i}"}
%[text] [⇦ Return to the main menu](file:../MainMenu.m)
%%
